5 â€¦ â€œWe will closely monitor how this change works in practice and adjust if needed.â€ The change is already visible in the upcoming Firefox Release Calendar. At the time of writing, it shows the current four-week cadence for Firefox 153 and 154, with Firefox 155 brought forward to September 1. From then on, it lists releases at roughly two-week intervals. This isnâ€™t unprecedented. The last time Mozilla did it was over a decade ago. Google announced a very similar change for Chrome back in March, and The Register reported on it going to six-weekly releases in 2010 and then four-weekly ones in 2021. Brace for the impact of the next ESR In the meantime, Firefox 153 is nearly here: at the time of writing, itâ€™s scheduled for Tuesday, July 21. Right now, the release notes are blank, but the beta release notes are more forthcoming. You can look forward to further improvements to PDF editing. Version 153 will be able to merge multiple PDF documents into one by a simple drag-and-drop in the PDF sidebar, and insert images into PDFs as new pages. It will also improve highlighting text in PDFs. The new version can generate QR codes for sharing web pages offline, such as in printed documents. It can verify and display the EUâ€™s new Qualified Website Authentication Certificates, or QWACs for short. These are part of the new eIDAS legislation, which is a slightly convoluted acronym for â€œelectronic IDentification, Authentication and trust Servicesâ€. Sounds cumbersome, but if it helps make the Wild West of the Web a bit safer, weâ€™re all for it. Another security tweak is that extensions will lose local-file access by default. As we use one that relies on it - the excellent Multithreaded Download Manager - that's slightly concerning, although users will be able to grant the permission separately, so we'll see. If a tab is using your location, Firefox 153 will highlight this with a map-pin icon in the address bar. The last release could recognize a few keywords in the address bar to mute all sound: this function will get extended, with typed commands for picking colors from pages, and accessing experimental â€œLabsâ€ features. Come back, Ubuntu Unity and your HUD, all is forgiven. Thereâ€™s also experimental JPEG XL support. Pop-up video player controls will work better, and if you use Windows and have a compatible GPU and drivers, 153 will play HDR video. On macOS, Firefox supports the Fn+F keystroke for switching to full-screen mode â€“ which means KeyboardControls.com has to update its description of the function. Firefox 153 will also be a significant release, because it will be the next ESR version: it will get security updates for at least 15 months, meaning until late 2027. (And maybe longer: Firefox 115 is still getting updates, and now will until March 2027.) In turn, that means that Firefox 153 is also the basis of the latest beta of the AI-free Waterfox fork, which recently integrated built-in ad blocking. Â®","Prior research (sites/koios.news/memory/_index.md, sha256:2fdd12ac39894400c92f8947f2adba68e10867fb1926cd0725e10d7d3d97d5a6): Internal planning now has `src/administrating/developing`, exposed in `/departments.json`, human board `/administrating/developing`, `/administrating/developing.json`, OpenAPI, and MCP tool `read_developing`. Its `topologyConstruction` section records the current upstream/content-derived plan for nested component topology: source-to-reference fibration, desk-chain nesting, article sheaf/cosheaf, newsroom swarm hands, semantic hypertext packets, and aperiodic dream budgeting. Semantic hypertext packets are now active for source-cycle repair packets and content revision packets through `.packet.html` routes with scriptless `data-e`/`data-a`/`data-v` cells. Aggregate ad-performance managemen...","Prior research (sites/koios.news/memory/_index.md, sha256:2fdd12ac39894400c92f8947f2adba68e10867fb1926cd0725e10d7d3d97d5a6): Draft-time same-site link guidance now sits before publication: `/operators/writing/internal-link-guidance.json`, `/operators/assignments/{assignmentId}/link-guidance.json`, MCP tool `read_draft_internal_link_guidance`, research-packet HTML, assignment work-order HTML, and assignment draft forms all expose published Koios article targets to consider while writing. This is composition guidance only: it excludes assignment source article slugs, does not create references, and must not be treated as factual support. - **The source cycle is an operator-visible production act.** `src/researching/sourcing/source-cycle.mts` reads `producing-content.config.json`, ingests Koios-owned newscable sou...","Prior research (sites/koios.news/memory/_index.md, sha256:2fdd12ac39894400c92f8947f2adba68e10867fb1926cd0725e10d7d3d97d5a6): The Koios wrapper snapshots existing manuscripts before the farm writes and restores any existing path collision, reporting those as `candidateWriteCollisions` so autonomous drafts cannot silently unpublish or overwrite shipped articles. Publication remains standards-gated. Failed candidate gates and intake obstructions now fold into read-only source-cycle repair packets at `/operators/source-cycle/repairs`, `/operators/source-cycle/repairs.json`, per-candidate `/operators/source-cycle/repairs/{slug}` and `/operators/source-cycle/repairs/{slug}.json`, operator workbench `sourceCycleRepairs`, and MCP tools `read_source_cycle_repairs`/`read_source_cycle_repair_packet`; packets preserve the...","Prior research (sites/koios.news/memory/_index.md, sha256:2fdd12ac39894400c92f8947f2adba68e10867fb1926cd0725e10d7d3d97d5a6): `/operators/manuscripts.json` gives the machine manuscript inventory: draft state, public URL, standards URL, publish URL, next work state, reference/word counts, and blocking findings per manuscript. Human operators have a dedicated manuscript queue at `/operators/manuscripts.html`, sorted by next editorial action while preserving `POST /operators/manuscripts` as the JSON draft-creation endpoint. Drafts are also ranked by publication distance at `/operators/publication-candidates` and `/operators/publication-candidates.json`, with workbench field `publicationCandidates` and MCP tool `read_publication_candidates`; this is a projection over standards reviews and source-cycle repair packets...","Prior research (sites/koios.news/memory/_index.md, sha256:2fdd12ac39894400c92f8947f2adba68e10867fb1926cd0725e10d7d3d97d5a6): Human operators have a dedicated manuscript queue at `/operators/manuscripts.html`, sorted by next editorial action while preserving `POST /operators/manuscripts` as the JSON draft-creation endpoint. Drafts are also ranked by publication distance at `/operators/publication-candidates` and `/operators/publication-candidates.json`, with workbench field `publicationCandidates` and MCP tool `read_publication_candidates`; this is a projection over standards reviews and source-cycle repair packets, not a new task store. A standards-clear draft with an open source-cycle repair packet is now an `editorial-hold` candidate with links to the repair packet, so source/reference/provenance work remains...","Prior research (sites/koios.news/memory/_index.md, sha256:2fdd12ac39894400c92f8947f2adba68e10867fb1926cd0725e10d7d3d97d5a6): `content/posts/acurite-delays-app-migration-due-to-user-concerns-over.md` was published through the new newsroom HTML publish flow on 2026-06-19 and the public site was redeployed. It now fails standards for malformed H2 headings and remains a revision target for no internal links, one reference, uncited bibliography, SEO-term overuse, and malformed H2 headings. `content/posts/uk-retail-sales-spike-masks-climate-driven-supply-fragility.md` (2026-06-19) was generated earlier by the source cycle from Koios's `collapse-finance` wire, human-edited for standards, converted to canonical CSL `references:` with `issued.date-parts`, and published through the standards gate after redeploy. It has e...","Prior research (sites/koios.news/memory/_index.md, sha256:2fdd12ac39894400c92f8947f2adba68e10867fb1926cd0725e10d7d3d97d5a6): ` body starts, then published through `POST /operators/manuscripts/world-cup-faces-air-quality-disaster-as-wildfires-threaten/publish` on 2026-06-19. It has `referenceCount: 2`, `draft: false`, `gates_clear: true`, and no standards findings. `content/posts/amazon-s-astro-and-the-energy-cost-of-giving.md` was generated by the 2026-06-19 source cycle from the `collapse-tech` wire after 19 new source records were written. The wrapper normalized two intake URLs into canonical CSL `references:` and added draft same-site link guidance. Human editing tightened the description and changed one H2 to include `AI infrastructure energy use`, then the article was published through `POST /operators/man...","Prior research (sites/koios.news/memory/_index.md, sha256:2fdd12ac39894400c92f8947f2adba68e10867fb1926cd0725e10d7d3d97d5a6): The `hello-world` article renders that A-Ads iframe from frontmatter under the fingerprint/banner image, and the public CSP/privacy policy recognize the A-Ads frame. - **The content and data stores are submodules.** Posts live in `content/posts/`; data lives in `data/`, with append-only traces under `data/logs/` and current JSON records under `data/records/`. - **The producing-content instance is configured in** `producing-content.config.json`: Koios's farm property, seed terms, beat sources, Search Console property, front-matter namespace, voice, gates, model, content store, and data store. `package.json` is package/site metadata, not the farm instance carrier. The seed vocabulary now ex...","Prior research (sites/koios.news/memory/_index.md, sha256:2fdd12ac39894400c92f8947f2adba68e10867fb1926cd0725e10d7d3d97d5a6): - The manual workshop references `scripts/new-post.mjs` and `scripts/lint-post.mjs`, but no `scripts/` directory is present in this package. Until restored, use the documented rules directly: frontmatter shape, >=800 body words, SEO term in first paragraph and a `##`, then `pnpm --dir sites/koios.news run check` plus local server probes. - The 2026-06-19 source cycle showed that Search Console demand pull still returns `403` for `sc-domain:koios.news`; until permissions are fixed, farm assignments come from seed/static demand rather than live search demand. - The 2026-06-19 source cycles showed assignment/story alignment problems: the farm paired `crypto mining energy demand` with a UK re...","Prior research (sites/koios.news/memory/_index.md, sha256:2fdd12ac39894400c92f8947f2adba68e10867fb1926cd0725e10d7d3d97d5a6): Until restored, use the documented rules directly: frontmatter shape, >=800 body words, SEO term in first paragraph and a `##`, then `pnpm --dir sites/koios.news run check` plus local server probes. - The 2026-06-19 source cycle showed that Search Console demand pull still returns `403` for `sc-domain:koios.news`; until permissions are fixed, farm assignments come from seed/static demand rather than live search demand. - The 2026-06-19 source cycles showed assignment/story alignment problems: the farm paired `crypto mining energy demand` with a UK retail heat story earlier, then paired `farmland and water rights` with a UK borrowing/water-shares market story. Human editing changed the lat...","Prior research (sites/koios.news/memory/_index.md, sha256:2fdd12ac39894400c92f8947f2adba68e10867fb1926cd0725e10d7d3d97d5a6): - The 2026-06-19 source cycles showed assignment/story alignment problems: the farm paired `crypto mining energy demand` with a UK retail heat story earlier, then paired `farmland and water rights` with a UK borrowing/water-shares market story. Human editing changed the latter SEO term to `UK borrowing and water shares` and narrowed the copy. Source-cycle repair packets now expose this friction from run traces, and operators can convert those packets into durable editing assignments. A repair assignment now exists for `ai-capital-expenditure-bubble` after an unsupported-demand obstruction. Future writing-flow work should make research packets or claim overlap gate the assignment before dr...","Prior research (sites/koios.news/memory/_index.md, sha256:2fdd12ac39894400c92f8947f2adba68e10867fb1926cd0725e10d7d3d97d5a6): A repair assignment now exists for `ai-capital-expenditure-bubble` after an unsupported-demand obstruction. Future writing-flow work should make research packets or claim overlap gate the assignment before drafting. - The escalated 2026-06-19 source cycle also exposed a slug/path collision: the farm tried to write a new `uk-bond-yields-rise-as-water-company-shares-fall` draft over a previously published article, temporarily reverting it to `draft: true` with no references. The article was restored, and the source-cycle wrapper now snapshots existing manuscripts, restores collided paths, skips post-processing for those candidates, and reports `candidateWriteCollisions`. Future upstream wor...","Prior research (src/content/assets/legacy/2026-07-03-koios.news/memory/_index.md, sha256:2fdd12ac39894400c92f8947f2adba68e10867fb1926cd0725e10d7d3d97d5a6): Internal planning now has `src/administrating/developing`, exposed in `/departments.json`, human board `/administrating/developing`, `/administrating/developing.json`, OpenAPI, and MCP tool `read_developing`. Its `topologyConstruction` section records the current upstream/content-derived plan for nested component topology: source-to-reference fibration, desk-chain nesting, article sheaf/cosheaf, newsroom swarm hands, semantic hypertext packets, and aperiodic dream budgeting. Semantic hypertext packets are now active for source-cycle repair packets and content revision packets through `.packet.html` routes with scriptless `data-e`/`data-a`/`data-v` cells. Aggregate ad-performance managemen...","Prior research (src/content/assets/legacy/2026-07-03-koios.news/memory/_index.md, sha256:2fdd12ac39894400c92f8947f2adba68e10867fb1926cd0725e10d7d3d97d5a6): Draft-time same-site link guidance now sits before publication: `/operators/