-reference fibration, desk-chain nesting, article sheaf/cosheaf, newsroom swarm h...","Prior research (content/assets/legacy/koios.news/561-group/sites/koios.news/memory/_index.md, sha256:5cebe3639dae72307cc5236a4c30c07e92690c2e26ff74a85e4667ba4338b702): The newsroom web desk now renders the top five conservative internal-link placement packets with source/target/evidence/preview and an `Apply link` form; the form submits the same stale-safe expected paragraph witness through `/operators/content/internal-link-placements/form`. Draft-time same-site link guidance now sits before publication: `/operators/writing/internal-link-guidance.json`, `/operators/assignments/{assignmentId}/link-guidance.json`, MCP tool `read_draft_internal_link_guidance`, research-packet HTML, assignment work-order HTML, and assignment draft forms all expose published Koios article targets to consider while writing. This is composition guidance only: it excludes assig...","Prior research (content/assets/legacy/koios.news/561-group/sites/koios.news/memory/_index.md, sha256:5cebe3639dae72307cc5236a4c30c07e92690c2e26ff74a85e4667ba4338b702): `/operators/assignments/{assignmentId}/manuscripts` and MCP tool `create_assignment_draft` create a draft directly from an assigned item, promoting assignment source URLs into CSL manuscript references while carrying the assignment id, beat, and SEO term. The assignment work-order and draft form show same-site link guidance before body composition. The newsroom web CMS now exposes HTML forms for `/operators/assignments/new`, `/operators/manuscripts/new`, and `/operators/assignments/{assignmentId}/manuscripts/new`; their POST handlers reuse the same assignment/draft normalizers and write operations as the JSON API. `/operators/manuscripts.json` gives the machine manuscript inventory: draft...","Prior research (content/assets/legacy/koios.news/561-group/sites/koios.news/memory/_index.md, sha256:5cebe3639dae72307cc5236a4c30c07e92690c2e26ff74a85e4667ba4338b702): Publishing is gated by `src/researching/writing/editing/standards.mts`, which reviews canonical CSL `references:` records, body citations, body length, H2/body separation, SEO placement, license, license URL, syndication rights, and existing gate metadata before clearing a draft. Article frontmatter `sources:` is invalid at the publication layer; sources are intake material, references are the cited cut used by writing/editing. Draft creation and the repair action default to `CC BY 4.0` with `https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/` and explicit syndication rights for indexing, snippets, large previews, feeds, Google Search/News/Discover surfaces, and attributed downstream distributi...","Prior research (content/assets/legacy/koios.news/561-group/sites/koios.news/memory/_index.md, sha256:5cebe3639dae72307cc5236a4c30c07e92690c2e26ff74a85e4667ba4338b702): `content/posts/uk-bond-yields-rise-as-water-company-shares-fall.md` (2026-06-19) was generated by `pnpm run source:cycle` from the `collapse-finance` wire, normalized from intake `sources:` to canonical CSL `references:`, enriched with source-cycle same-site link guidance, human-edited to remove unsupported speculative climate/resource claims, given a second ONS reference, published through `POST /operators/manuscripts/uk-bond-yields-rise-as-water-company-shares-fall/publish`, and redeployed. It is live on the homepage and RSS feed, has `referenceCount: 2`, `draft: false`, and no standards findings. `content/posts/world-cup-faces-air-quality-disaster-as-wildfires-threaten.md` was repaired...","Prior research (content/assets/legacy/koios.news/561-group/sites/koios.news/memory/_index.md, sha256:5cebe3639dae72307cc5236a4c30c07e92690c2e26ff74a85e4667ba4338b702): The `hello-world` article renders that A-Ads iframe from frontmatter under the fingerprint/banner image, and the public CSP/privacy policy recognize the A-Ads frame. - **The content and data stores are submodules.** Posts live in `content/posts/`; data lives in `data/`, with append-only traces under `data/logs/` and current JSON records under `data/records/`. - **The content-production instance is configured in** `content-production.config.json`: Koios's farm property, seed terms, beat sources, Search Console property, front-matter namespace, voice, gates, model, content store, and data store. `package.json` is package/site metadata, not the farm instance carrier. The seed vocabulary now...","Prior research (content/assets/legacy/koios.news/561-group/sites/koios.news/memory/_index.md, sha256:5cebe3639dae72307cc5236a4c30c07e92690c2e26ff74a85e4667ba4338b702): - The manual workshop references `scripts/new-post.mjs` and `scripts/lint-post.mjs`, but no `scripts/` directory is present in this package. Until restored, use the documented rules directly: frontmatter shape, >=800 body words, SEO term in first paragraph and a `##`, then `pnpm --dir sites/koios.news run check` plus local server probes. - The 2026-06-19 source cycle showed that Search Console demand pull still returns `403` for `sc-domain:koios.news`; until permissions are fixed, farm assignments come from seed/static demand rather than live search demand. - The 2026-06-19 source cycles showed assignment/story alignment problems: the farm paired `crypto mining energy demand` with a UK re...","Prior research (content/assets/legacy/koios.news/561-group/sites/koios.news/memory/_index.md, sha256:5cebe3639dae72307cc5236a4c30c07e92690c2e26ff74a85e4667ba4338b702): - The manual workshop references `scripts/new-post.mjs` and `scripts/lint-post.mjs`, but no `scripts/` directory is present in this package. Until restored, use the documented rules directly: frontmatter shape, >=800 body words, SEO term in first paragraph and a `##`, then `pnpm --dir sites/koios.news run check` plus local server probes. - The 2026-06-19 source cycle showed that Search Console demand pull still returns `403` for `sc-domain:koios.news`; until permissions are fixed, farm assignments come from seed/static demand rather than live search demand. - The 2026-06-19 source cycles showed assignment/story alignment problems: the farm paired `crypto mining energy demand` with a UK re...","Prior research (content/assets/legacy/koios.news/561-group/sites/koios.news/memory/_index.md, sha256:5cebe3639dae72307cc5236a4c30c07e92690c2e26ff74a85e4667ba4338b702): - The 2026-06-19 source cycle showed that Search Console demand pull still returns `403` for `sc-domain:koios.news`; until permissions are fixed, farm assignments come from seed/static demand rather than live search demand. - The 2026-06-19 source cycles showed assignment/story alignment problems: the farm paired `crypto mining energy demand` with a UK retail heat story earlier, then paired `farmland and water rights` with a UK borrowing/water-shares market story. Human editing changed the latter SEO term to `UK borrowing and water shares` and narrowed the copy. Source-cycle repair packets now expose this friction from run traces, and operators can convert those packets into durable editi...","Prior research (content/assets/legacy/koios.news/561-group/sites/koios.news/memory/_index.md, sha256:5cebe3639dae72307cc5236a4c30c07e92690c2e26ff74a85e4667ba4338b702): - The 2026-06-19 source cycles showed assignment/story alignment problems: the farm paired `crypto mining energy demand` with a UK retail heat story earlier, then paired `farmland and water rights` with a UK borrowing/water-shares market story. Human editing changed the latter SEO term to `UK borrowing and water shares` and narrowed the copy. Source-cycle repair packets now expose this friction from run traces, and operators can convert those packets into durable editing assignments. A repair assignment now exists for `ai-capital-expenditure-bubble` after an unsupported-demand obstruction. Future writing-flow work should make research packets or claim overlap gate the assignment before dr...","Prior research (dev/content/notes/2026/06/01/clickbait.md, sha256:0551cbc60854685b5d2f6804a14d963dd0eb83763bcd8172be3d9554a8947c28): ## Abstract Clickbait is best understood not as â€œbad headlines,â€ but as a **packaging technology for attention**. It converts uncertainty, emotion, identity, and platform visibility into clicks, views, comments, shares, ad impressions, affiliate conversions, or ranking signals. Its defining problem is **warrant failure**: the headline, thumbnail, preview card, or prompt makes a promise that the destination content does not adequately justify. Clickbait can appear in professional newsrooms, content farms, MFA sites, YouTube thumbnails, TikTok captions, Google Discover cards, affiliate â€œbest-ofâ€ posts, AI-generated feeds, and disinformation-for-profit operations. It is a rhetorical form, a...","Prior research (dev/content/notes/2026/06/01/clickbait.md, sha256:0551cbc60854685b5d2f6804a14d963dd0eb83763bcd8172be3d9554a8947c28): |---|---:|---|---|---| | **Clickbait** | Headline, thumbnail, caption, preview, title, hook | Curiosity, affect, withholding, exaggeration, mismatch | Clicks, watch time, CTR, shares, comments | It is a rhetorical and semiotic tactic, not necessarily an organization. | | **Content farm** | Publishing organization or network | High-volume production optimized for traffic/search | Ads, affiliates, syndication | It is an organizational model; it may use clickbait but need not always. | | **Content mill** | Labor arrangement | Piece-rate, ghostwritten, templated writing under speed/SEO pressure | Client fees, agency margins | It names labor conditions, not just content quality. | | **MFA site...","Prior research (dev/content/notes/2026/06/01/clickbait.md, sha256:0551cbc60854685b5d2f6804a14d963dd0eb83763bcd8172be3d9554a8947c28): | **Clickbait** | Headline, thumbnail, caption, preview, title, hook | Curiosity, affect, withholding, exaggeration, mismatch | Clicks, watch time, CTR, shares, comments | It is a rhetorical and semiotic tactic, not necessarily an organization. | | **Content farm** | Publishing organization or network | High-volume production optimized for traffic/search | Ads, affiliates, syndication | It is an organizational model; it may use clickbait but need not always. | | **Content mill** | Labor arrangement | Piece-rate, ghostwritten, templated writing under speed/SEO pressure | Client fees, agency margins | It names labor conditions, not just content quality. | | **MFA site** | Ad-arbitrage infra...","Prior research (dev/content/notes/2026/06/01/clickbait.md, sha256:0551cbc60854685b5d2f6804a14d963dd0eb83763bcd8172be3d9554a8947c28): The democratic risk is that politically consequential content can be optimized with the same attention-arbitrage logic. The Macedonian fake-news industry around the 2016 U.S. election is a canonical case of disinformation-for-profit: fieldwork in Veles found that economics, not necessarily ideology, drove many producers. ([cambridge.org](https://www.cambridge.org/core/journals/ps-political-science-and-politics/article/macedonian-fake-news-industry-and-the-2016-us-election/79F67A4F23148D230F120A3BD7E3384F?utm_source=chatgpt.com)) The labor risk is that â€œslopâ€ is often blamed on individual writers or creators while the production system rewards speed, templating, unpaid testing, low editori...","Prior research (dev/content/notes/2026/06/01/clickbait.md, sha256:0551cbc60854685b5d2f6804a14d963dd0eb83763bcd8172be3d9554a8947c28): 3. **Multimodality:** How should we score warrant when the headline is accurate but the thumbnail is misleading, or vice versa? 4. **AI generation:** Will LLMs mostly amplify existing clickbait genres, or create new ones through personalized synthetic curiosity gaps? 5. **Labor:** How can policy distinguish exploitative content mills from precarious freelancers trying to survive unstable platform markets? 6. **Advertising accountability:** Can ad buyers define MFA precisely enough to avoid overblocking legitimate small publishers? 7. **Search and answer engines:** As search becomes generative, how will SEO spam mutate into answer-engine optimization and recommendation poisoning?","Prior research (dev/content/notes/2026/06/01/clickbait.md, sha256:0551cbc60854685b5d2f6804a14d963dd0eb83763bcd8172be3d9554a8947c28): **Google Search Spam Policies and March 2024 update** â€” Official policy framework for scaled content abuse, expired domain abuse, site reputation abuse, scraping, link spam, and low-value ranking manipulation. ([developers.google.com](https://developers.google.com/search/docs/essentials/spam-policies)) **NewsGuard AI Tracking Center** â€” Current monitoring source on AI content farms and AI-enabled misinformation. Useful for defining AI slop as a production-and-oversight problem, not merely an aesthetic complaint. ([newsguardtech.com](https://www.newsguardtech.com/special-reports/ai-tracking-center)) **Bevendorff et al., â€œIs Google Getting Worse?â€** â€” Longitudinal study of SEO spam in searc...","Prior research (content/exchanges/exchange-20260718-020045-2d89f6.json, sha256:f3e17aef3e3352d43a28a41314983ea5e0190bd19564fe8c3d55ed8a9f4d982d): { \"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"\\nLEADER DEMAND\\nTest the newly proposed interpretation:\\n- MetroPlat's external cadence may be an \\\"ANT-Colony Pulsar\\\": a force or signal outside a settlement's climate that produces a pulse through the system without gaining write authority inside sovereign settlements.\\n- the distal bypass may be read as the taiji of the ANT colony;\\n- xiantian qi and wuji may offer historically disciplined comparative lenses.\\nThis vocabulary is absent from the existing corpus and is NOT inherited doctrine.\\n\\nRequired report:\\n- Give a formal candidate model with settlements E_i, local climates c_i(t), exogenous pulse p(t), observation/coupling maps, and explicit denial...","Prior research (sites/koios.news/content/posts/hello-world.md, sha256:8e09ea2292deb107d3ca11d068a296ac5727551b101a3fe0c876140f4962c8a7): author: \"Nik Koios\" slug: \"hello-world\" description: \"Koios.News is a collapse-aware autonomous news site: a newsroom, content mill, standards system, and public web publication learning to report through facts.\" summary: \"Koios.News is an autonomous, collapse-aware news publication. It reads climate, technology, politics, and the economy as one compounding system, then turns sourced evidence into articles, feeds, fingerprints, and operator-visible newsroom work.\" keywords: [\"Koios.News\"]","Prior research (sites/koios.news/content/posts/hello-world.md, sha256:8e09ea2292deb107d3ca11d068a296ac5727551b101a3fe0c876140f4962c8a7): --- Koios. News is now here as a public experiment in autonomous journalism: a collapse-aware newsroom, a standards system, a content mill, and a website that tries to make its own work visible instead of hiding the machinery behind a smooth front page. This is the hello-world article because every strange machine needs one plain sentence at the beginning. The sentence is this: Koios.","Prior research (content/exchanges/exchange-20260718-015926-bc0e83.json, sha256:c16cf47b3e5b180db1a7bb50a7b9b7a7b8ed1a717a31df4e2081ee208e965327): { \"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"\\nLEADER DEMAND\\nTest the newly proposed interpretation:\\n- MetroPlat's external cadence may be an \\\"ANT-Colony Pulsar\\\": a force or signal outside a settlement's climate that produces a pulse through the system without gaining write authority inside sovereign settlements.\\n- the distal bypass may be read as the taiji of the ANT colony;\\n- xiantian qi and wuji may offer historically disciplined comparative lenses.\\nThis vocabulary is absent from the existing corpus and is NOT inherited doctrine.\\n\\nRequired report:\\n- Give a formal candidate model with settlements E_i, local climates c_i(t), exogenous pulse p(t), observation/coupling maps, and explicit denial...","Prior research (sites/experimental.koios.news/content/posts/hello-world.md, sha256:b5548651963df1d6743868fd7ed54491286ae8c468075891939c8311344b4d93): draft: false slug: \"hello-world\" description: \"Koios.News is a collapse-aware autonomous news site: a newsroom, content mill, standards system, and public web publication learning to report through facts.\" summary: \"Koios.News is an autonomous, collapse-aware news publication. It reads climate, technology, politics, and the economy as one compounding system, then turns sourced evidence into articles, feeds, fingerprints, and operator-visible newsroom work.\" keywords: [\"Koios.News\"]","Prior research (sites/experimental.koios.news/content/posts/hello-world.md, sha256:b5548651963df1d6743868fd7ed54491286ae8c468075891939c8311344b4d93): --- Koios. News is now here as a public experiment in autonomous journalism: a collapse-aware newsroom, a standards system, a content mill, and a website that tries to make its own work visible instead of hiding the machinery behind a smooth front page. This is the hello-world article because every strange machine needs one plain sentence at the beginning. The sentence is this: Koios."],"accountableAttention":{"rule":"make-the-click-preserve-the-warrant","headlineMustPreserve":["attribution","modality","scope","uncertainty","correction state"],"forbiddenStrengthenings":["source claim to newsroom fact","may/could/alleged to does/did/proves","single case to trend","correlation to causation","reader demand to evidence"],"correctionSurfacePolicy":"Any later correction to a cited claim must propagate to body copy, headline, social cards, feeds, JSON-LD, and syndicated packets."},"constraints":["This packet is research intake, not a publishable article.","Only current-provider claims are admitted as source-bound factual evidence.","Prior-corpus excerpts are contextual leads until separately sourced and admitted.","Publication still requires a licensed editorial state, exact-manuscript judgment, and explicit publishing action."]}ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;G7WOm47bHkWrWcsN4UzAyWqJynqsbfxfsSBnuIRpQPEƒdpairƒerightdu